# Copy to .env and fill in. These are PUBLIC build-time values, safe to commit —
# privacy is enforced by RLS, not by hiding the anon key.
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://<project-ref>.supabase.co
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=<anon-key>

# --- Secrets (do NOT put these in .env — put them in .env.local, which is
#     git-ignored via the .env*.local pattern). Non-EXPO_PUBLIC_ so they are
#     never inlined into the app bundle; used only by the Node smoke/seed script. ---
# Copy the block below into .env.local:
#   OWNER_EMAIL=owner@example.com
#   OWNER_PASSWORD=<owner-password>

# --- AI provider key (F-02) — NOT an env var here. ---
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY lives only as a Supabase Edge Function secret, so it never
# reaches the client bundle or this repo:
#   npx supabase secrets set ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=<key>
# The app calls the `estimate` function (via src/data/estimation.ts) and never
# sees the key. Do not add it to .env or .env.local.
